<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/13th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">First Mongol invasion of Burma</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1277">1277</a>–<a href="/years/1287">1287</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The First Mongol invasion of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burma">Burma</a> was the series of campaigns from 1277 to 1287 by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yuan-dynasty">Yuan dynasty</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kublai-khan">Kublai Khan</a> against the Pagan Kingdom. After a battle at Ngasaunggyan (1277) and further invasions, Mongol forces reached the Pagan heartland in 1287; the kingdom broke apart after King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/narathihapate">Narathihapate</a> was assassinated, ending more than two centuries of Pagan rule over the Irrawaddy valley.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/first-mongol-invasion-of-burma.jpg" alt="First Mongol invasion of Burma" width="320" height="634" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Hybernator · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mongol_invasions_of_Burma_(1277-87).png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
